00:15:25.827 --> 00:15:27.747
and email in your receipt
so we can keep track.

00:15:27.747 --> 00:15:29.540
Thank you guys so much for watching.

00:15:29.540 --> 00:15:32.796
Continue to believe or
whatever your one word is

00:15:32.796 --> 00:15:34.447
and I'll see you soon.

00:15:34.447 --> 00:15:37.197
(dramatic music)

00:15:40.471 --> 00:15:43.158
- And let me tell you,
you should feel so proud

00:15:43.158 --> 00:15:45.596
of making it to this day

00:15:45.596 --> 00:15:49.789
and I hope that you're
excited to get started

00:15:49.789 --> 00:15:52.707
on that next chapter, but I also imagine

00:15:52.707 --> 00:15:55.979
that you might think
about all of that history,

00:15:55.979 --> 00:15:59.229
all those heroes who came before you

00:15:59.229 --> 00:16:03.536
and you might also feel a
little pressure, you know.

00:16:03.536 --> 00:16:06.163
Pressure to live up to the legacy of those

00:16:06.163 --> 00:16:08.169
who came before you.

00:16:08.169 --> 00:16:12.072
Pressure to meet the
expectations of others.

00:16:12.072 --> 00:16:14.214
And believe me, I understand
that kind of pressure.

00:16:14.214 --> 00:16:17.434
(audience laughing)

00:16:17.434 --> 00:16:19.212
I've experienced a
little bit of it myself.

00:16:19.212 --> 00:16:22.198
(audience applauses)

00:16:22.198 --> 00:16:24.296
You see graduates, I didn't start out

00:16:24.296 --> 00:16:28.918
as the full formed First Lady
who stands before you today.

00:16:28.918 --> 00:16:33.435
No, no, I had my share
of bumps along the way.

00:16:33.435 --> 00:16:34.907
Back when my husband first started

00:16:34.907 --> 00:16:36.649
campaigning for president,

00:16:36.649 --> 00:16:39.478
folks had all sorts of questions of me.

00:16:39.478 --> 00:16:42.038
What kind of First Lady would I be?

00:16:42.038 --> 00:16:44.207
What kinds of issues would I take on?

00:16:44.207 --> 00:16:46.569
Would I be more like Laura
Bush or Hilary Clinton

00:16:46.569 --> 00:16:47.902
or Nancy Reagan?

00:16:48.905 --> 00:16:50.749
And the truth is those same questions

00:16:50.749 --> 00:16:53.700
would have been posed to
any candidate's spouse.

00:16:53.700 --> 00:16:56.081
That's just the way the process works.

00:16:56.081 --> 00:16:59.994
But as potentially the first
African American First Lady,

00:16:59.994 --> 00:17:03.742
I was also the focus of
another set of questions

00:17:03.742 --> 00:17:07.305
and speculations,
conversations sometimes rooted

00:17:07.305 --> 00:17:10.782
in the fears and misperceptions of others.

00:17:10.782 --> 00:17:15.105
Was I too loud or too
angry or too emasculating?

00:17:15.105 --> 00:17:19.272
(audience applauses)
Or was I too soft?

00:17:21.075 --> 00:17:22.785
Too much of a mom?

00:17:22.785 --> 00:17:24.649
Not enough of a career woman?

00:17:24.649 --> 00:17:28.816
Then there was the first time
I was on a magazine cover.

00:17:31.217 --> 00:17:33.289
It was a cartoon drawing of me

00:17:33.289 --> 00:17:36.206
with a huge Afro and a machine gun.

00:17:37.398 --> 00:17:42.339
Now yeah, it was satire but
if I'm really being honest

00:17:42.339 --> 00:17:45.078
that knocked me back a bit.

00:17:45.078 --> 00:17:49.245
It made me wonder, well, just
how are people seeing me?

00:17:50.601 --> 00:17:53.485
Or you might remember the
onstage celebratory fist bump

00:17:53.485 --> 00:17:56.243
between me and my husband
after a primary win

00:17:56.243 --> 00:17:59.993
that was referred to as
a terrorist fist jab.

00:18:01.295 --> 00:18:03.088
And over the years, folks have used plenty

00:18:03.088 --> 00:18:06.198
of interesting words to describe me.

00:18:06.198 --> 00:18:10.198
One said I exhibited a
little bit of uppity-ism.

00:18:11.105 --> 00:18:12.634
Another noted that I was one

00:18:12.634 --> 00:18:15.819
of my husband's cronies of color.

00:18:15.819 --> 00:18:19.986
Cable news charmingly referred
to me as Obama's baby mama.

00:18:22.005 --> 00:18:24.757
And, of course, Barack
has endured his fair share

00:18:24.757 --> 00:18:26.674
of insults and slights.

00:18:27.572 --> 00:18:30.239
Even today there are still folks

00:18:31.288 --> 00:18:33.621
questioning his citizenship.

00:18:35.303 --> 00:18:38.720
And all of this used to really get to me.

00:18:40.543 --> 00:18:43.918
Back in those days, I had
a lot of sleepless nights

00:18:43.918 --> 00:18:46.147
worrying about what people thought of me,

00:18:46.147 --> 00:18:49.043
wondering if I might be
hurting my husband's chances

00:18:49.043 --> 00:18:51.496
of winning his election,

00:18:51.496 --> 00:18:53.223
fearing how my girls would feel

00:18:53.223 --> 00:18:55.250
if they found out what some people

00:18:55.250 --> 00:18:57.583
were saying about their mom,

00:18:58.663 --> 00:19:02.346
but eventually I realized that if I wanted

00:19:02.346 --> 00:19:06.263
to keep my sanity and
not let others define me,

00:19:07.217 --> 00:19:10.666
there was only one thing I could do

00:19:10.666 --> 00:19:13.881
and that was to have faith
in God's plan for me.

00:19:13.881 --> 00:19:16.441
(cheering)

00:19:16.441 --> 00:19:19.108
I had to ignore all of the noise

00:19:20.051 --> 00:19:24.218
and be true to myself and the
rest would work itself out.

00:19:26.843 --> 00:19:30.287
- Because we know how difficult
your husband's job is.

00:19:30.287 --> 00:19:32.915
What are the difficulties
of being the First Lady?

00:19:32.915 --> 00:19:35.834
- You know, I find it really hard,

00:19:35.834 --> 00:19:37.576
in the face of what he's going through

00:19:37.576 --> 00:19:40.954
and what I see happening to
folks when they're struggling,

00:19:40.954 --> 00:19:43.814
for me to even begin to complain.

00:19:43.814 --> 00:19:46.871
I have the best job because I don't

00:19:46.871 --> 00:19:49.203
have to make the hard decisions.

00:19:49.203 --> 00:19:51.031
The issues that I pick are ones

00:19:51.031 --> 00:19:52.592
that I feel passionately about.

00:19:52.592 --> 00:19:54.267
I get to pick and choose what I do

00:19:54.267 --> 00:19:57.167
which is why, you know, I love what I do.

00:19:57.167 --> 00:19:59.170
I get to spend time in this country

00:19:59.170 --> 00:20:00.753
traveling around, meeting--

00:20:00.753 --> 00:20:01.625
You see me.

00:20:01.625 --> 00:20:03.105
I'm jumping rope and hula hooping.

00:20:03.105 --> 00:20:06.105
(audience laughing)

00:20:07.793 --> 00:20:09.185
- [Barack] It's true.

00:20:09.185 --> 00:20:12.005
- So it's hard for me knowing, you know,

00:20:12.005 --> 00:20:16.981
how, you know, what struggle
is to even answer that

00:20:16.981 --> 00:20:18.690
with a straight face.

00:20:18.690 --> 00:20:20.483
You know, one of the things that I always,

00:20:20.483 --> 00:20:22.193
I tell my mentees, I tell my daughters,

00:20:22.193 --> 00:20:25.836
is that our first job in
life as women, I think,

00:20:25.836 --> 00:20:27.756
is to get to know ourselves

00:20:27.756 --> 00:20:31.923
and I think a lot of times
we don't do that (chuckles).

00:20:33.054 --> 00:20:35.543
We spend our time pleasing, satisfying,

00:20:35.543 --> 00:20:38.814
looking out into the world
to define who we are,

00:20:38.814 --> 00:20:41.679
listening to the messages, the images,

00:20:41.679 --> 00:20:45.214
the limited definitions that
people have of who we are

00:20:45.214 --> 00:20:48.396
and that's true for
women of color, for sure.

00:20:48.396 --> 00:20:51.813
There is a limited box that we are put in

00:20:52.818 --> 00:20:55.808
and if we live by that limited definition,

00:20:55.808 --> 00:20:58.817
we miss out on a lot of who we are

00:20:58.817 --> 00:21:02.723
but it takes taking the
time to know who you are

00:21:02.723 --> 00:21:05.806
to be able to deal with the onslaught

00:21:07.015 --> 00:21:10.932
of negative messages
that you're bound to get.

00:21:10.932 --> 00:21:13.756
So for me, I came into this

00:21:13.756 --> 00:21:16.673
with a pretty clear sense of myself

00:21:18.165 --> 00:21:19.818
and some of that comes with age,

00:21:19.818 --> 00:21:21.421
some of that comes with experience,

00:21:21.421 --> 00:21:23.957
some of that comes from
being fortune enough

00:21:23.957 --> 00:21:26.805
to have been raised by a loving mother,

00:21:26.805 --> 00:21:31.138
strong, focused, and a
father who loved me dearly

00:21:31.138 --> 00:21:34.555
so I fortunately came into this situation

00:21:35.511 --> 00:21:38.409
with a really clear sense of who I was.

